In addition, you will need the following:
1.  +5.0V @ 7.0 A power supply
2.  1 LG411 wirewrap board

The following are clarifications of what is contained in the dip list above.
1.  1 dip-oscillator, crystal, 32MHz (currently), TTL output
2.  There are a couple dummies which get wired for appropriate 11-bus connections
    They are explained in the drawings.
3.  The dipswitches are used to set the host identification numbers.
4.  There will be a small piece of circuitry, not yet designed, which will
    actually connect to the net cable.  It will probably have an opto-isolator
    and some linear components.  This part will have to wait a while.
